(0) One may NOT include blank sheets or sheets on which one has not attempt=
ed anything or done any work.

(1) One may NOT submit INCOMPLETE work for any part of any problem. One may=
 finish a part of a problem (marked as such) completely. But one must prove=
 EVERY assertion and check EVERY answer.

(2) One must draw every straight-line segment (including matrix brackets, c=
onclusion-bars, and so on) except for symbols explicitly excluded, visibly =
straight, using a ruler or appropriate software.

(3) On any sheet on which a problem occurs, one must fill in every blank an=
d perform any other action required. If the answer to some question such as=
 'why?' does not fit in the space provided in one's normal handwriting, one=
 must write it on the next page numbered properly.

(4) One may NOT make any extraneous marks anywhere on the exam.

(5) One may NOT use any undefined symbol or terminology.

(6) One may NOT use decimals, except if a problem requires one to do so.

(7) One may NOT use dots to mean multiplication, one must instead use paren=
theses and juxtaposition.

